<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · river</p><h1 class="enc-title">River Welland</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The River Welland rises in Northamptonshire in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/midlands">English Midlands</a> and flows north-east past Market Harborough, Stamford and Spalding to the Wash. For much of its course it forms county boundaries, and its valley was one of the early <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bantustan">homelands</a> of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/middle-angles">Middle Angles</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/river-welland.jpg" alt="River Welland" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:River_Welland.18.6.05.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
